## Step 1: Clean and validate (do this first, and report findings to me)
- Trim whitespace in text columns. Check for duplicate App Ids.
- Count apps with a blank or "Not Found" App Type, missing manager, or missing stage.
- Recompute these from the raw table and compare with the "Dashboard" sheet. List every mismatch. Known suspects: "Apps w/ Findings" shows 0, "Sonar Failing" equals total apps, "Apps by App Type" totals don't match total apps, "EOL <= 90 Days" equals "Approaching EOL".
- Put these findings in a final appendix slide titled "Data quality notes".

## Step 2: Derived metrics
- Total Findings per app = Codeql Warning + Codeql Error + MEND Critical + MEND Medium + Secret Scanning
- Risk Score per app = MEND Critical×10 + Secret Scanning×10 + Codeql Error×3 + MEND Medium×1 + Codeql Warning×0.5 + 15 if Days to TLM Target <= 90
- Risk Tier: High >= 25, Medium 8–24, Low 1–7, None 0
- App "at risk" = MEND Critical > 0 OR Secret Scanning > 0 OR Days to TLM Target <= 90
- Findings per app by manager (normalize for portfolio size)
- Sonar coverage % = apps with a real Sonar Key / total apps
- EOL buckets: Past EOL, 0–90 days, 91–180, 181–365, 1 year+, No EOL date

